# examples/spec/fastpaxos.cml: Fast Paxos as an abstract model,
# extending the shared consensus base.  Fast Paxos lets clients send
# values directly to acceptors in a "fast round", saving a message
# delay, at the cost that a fast round may COLLIDE (acceptors accept
# different values).  Its distinctive safety result is the fast-quorum
# size bound: a fast round is safe only if the fast quorum F exceeds
# 3N/4, so that a recovery coordinator reading a classic quorum can
# always resolve a collision unambiguously.
#
# Reference: Leslie Lamport, "Fast Paxos", Distributed Computing 19(2),
#   2006.  The bound F > 3N/4 comes from requiring every classic quorum
#   to intersect every pair of fast quorums (the triple intersection
#   that resolves a collision across rounds).
#
# The model has two rounds.  Round 0 is fast: each acceptor accepts one
# value directly (a collision is allowed).  A value is "fast-chosen" if
# a fast quorum of F acceptors accepted it.  Round 1 is a classic
# recovery: a coordinator reads a classic quorum (majority) of the
# fast-round state and re-proposes.  The recovery rule must carry
# forward any value that could have been fast-chosen: it proposes value
# v if v appears often enough in its read quorum that v might hold a
# fast quorum (the read quorum cannot rule it out).  A value is chosen
# if it is fast-chosen OR the recovery commits it.
#
# Safety (Agreement, inherited) requires that recovery never commits a
# value different from one that was fast-chosen.  With F > 3N/4 the read
# quorum always intersects a fast quorum in a majority of that fast
# quorum, so a fast-chosen value is unambiguous and recovery preserves
# it.  Here A = 5: a classic majority is 3, and 3N/4 = 3.75, so a
# correct fast quorum is F = 4.
#
# -DBUG: the fast quorum is shrunk to a plain majority (F = 3 <= 3N/4),
# so a collided fast round (value 1 on three acceptors, value 2 on two)
# lets recovery commit value 2 while value 1 was fast-chosen by its
# three -- two values chosen.
#
#   cmc --spec examples/spec/fastpaxos.cml
#   cmc --spec examples/spec/fastpaxos.cml --define BUG   (fast quorum shrunk)

module fastpaxos
extends consensus

const A = 5                     # acceptors 0 .. A-1
const QC = 3                    # classic quorum (majority of A)
const F = 4                     # fast quorum, > 3A/4 for safety

# acc[a] = the value acceptor a accepted in the fast round (0 = none).
var acc : [0 .. A-1 -> 0 .. V]
# committed = the value the recovery round committed (0 = none yet).
var committed : 0 .. V

init acc == [a in 0 .. A-1 -> 0]
init committed == 0

# fast round: an acceptor accepts a value directly from a client.
action fast(a in 0 .. A-1, v in 1 .. V):
  when acc[a] == 0
  acc' = [acc except [a] = v]

# a value is chosen if a fast quorum accepted it in the fast round.
action choose_fast(v in 1 .. V):
  when (count a in 0 .. A-1 : acc[a] == v) >= F
  chosen' = [chosen except [v] = 1]

# recovery round: a coordinator reads a classic quorum and commits a
# value v only if v COULD still be fast-chosen as far as its read can
# tell -- that is, v's acceptances plus the acceptors it did not read
# could reach a fast quorum: (count acc==v) + (A - QC) >= F.  With a
# correct fast quorum F > 3A/4 this holds for at most one value once the
# round is settled, so recovery cannot pick a value different from a
# fast-chosen one.  Committing is recorded both in `committed` and in
# `chosen` (a committed value is chosen).
action recover(v in 1 .. V):
  when committed == 0 and (count a in 0 .. A-1 : acc[a] == v) + (A - QC) >= F
  committed' = v
  chosen' = [chosen except [v] = 1]

# the planted bug: recovery treats the fast round as if a classic
# majority (QC) sufficed to choose, rather than a fast quorum (F).  With
# the smaller threshold a collided fast round lets recovery commit a
# value different from the one a fast quorum actually holds -- two values
# chosen.  (This is the "used a plain majority for the fast round"
# mistake the F > 3A/4 bound exists to prevent.)
action recover_bug(v in 1 .. V) [BUG]:
  when committed == 0 and (count a in 0 .. A-1 : acc[a] == v) + (A - QC) >= QC
  committed' = v
  chosen' = [chosen except [v] = 1]
